{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.678 accuracy at 5.90 GPU hours, establishing a baseline. With only one data point, the largest single architectural lever for improving accuracy is the image encoder quality — resnet50 (~25M params) is substantially weaker than imagenet_vit_l (~307M params), and in multimodal cellular profiling the image modality often carries critical morphological features. Question tested: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to ViT-L (while holding all other config_018 settings constant) meaningfully improve validation accuracy? This is a clean one-variable comparison that isolates the image encoder's contribution. Why this is the best next experiment: It has the highest expected accuracy gain of any single change available, and if it succeeds, it validates a large family of ViT-L-based configurations (config_008, 022, 029, 032, etc.) for subsequent exploitation. If it does not help, it tells me the bottleneck is elsewhere (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion) and I can redirect. Expected relative cost: ViT-L is roughly 3–4× the parameter count of resnet50, so I estimate ~9–12 GPU hours (moderately more expensive than config_018's 5.90), but well within the remaining budget for 8 experiments."
}

